@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps_landscape.component.loading_state a ds:Component;
    ds:name "Loading State";
    ds:summary "Loading State is an indeterminate status indicator with an off-screen `Loading...` label and a spinning Canonical icon hidden from assistive technology. It renders either a compact inline `<span role=\"status\">` or an outer `<div>` containing a Vanilla strip with centered spinner content.\n\nEvery non-inline rendering has the same outer wrapper. `centerOnScreen` only conditionally adds the CSS-module class that gives that wrapper full-viewport-height centering and padding. The component reports no percentage, accepts no custom message, and adds no focus target.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "node:\n  uri: ds:apps_landscape.component.loading_state\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        role: contained-mode outer wrapper\n        styles:\n          size.height: 100vh when centerOnScreen is truthy\n          spacing.padding: 1rem when centerOnScreen is truthy\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              semantic: status\n              role: contained loading status\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    role: centered status content\n                    edges:\n                      - node:\n                          role: accessible loading label\n                          relation:\n                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                      - node:\n                          uri: global.component.icon\n                          role: indeterminate spinner\n                          relation:\n                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"0..1\"\n          condition: inline is falsy\n    - node:\n        semantic: status\n        role: inline loading status\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: accessible loading label\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n          - node:\n              uri: global.component.icon\n              role: indeterminate spinner\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"0..1\"\n          condition: inline is truthy";
    ds:anatomyClassic "https://www.figma.com/design/I4WpvwMuQI6v1qhgUl63Sx/Landscape-Pragma-components?node-id=25-74&t=iG2ObZ6Q1XG2A2MB-4\n\nTable 37\n\n";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\n**Wait for asynchronous content**\n\nIndicate that a region or page is waiting for indeterminate asynchronous work before stable content can render.\n\n**Signal route redirection**\n\nCompose the separate Redirecting component, which uses `LoadingState inline`, when visible route-transition wording is required.\n\n**Compact pending values**\n\nUse the inline variant where a count, status, or small content fragment is pending and a strip would disrupt its surrounding layout.\n\n### When not to use\n\n**Report determinate progress**\n\nDisplaying a progress percentage or completion count for known-length operations.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using Loading State with a custom message or label to show “50% complete” or similar measured progress.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use a dedicated progress component (e.g., Vanilla Framework progress bar) when a percentage, count, or known total is available.\n\n**Load a button action**\n\nIndicating pending work initiated by a button click.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Wrapping a button in a Loading State div while its action awaits completion, disconnecting the status from the initiating control.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use the Button component’s native loading prop or disabled state so the pending status remains visually associated with the control that triggered it.\n\n**Explain a long operation**\n\nIndicating an extended wait without context about what is happening or why.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Rendering only the spinner with a generic “Loading…” message when a multi-minute operation is in progress, without explaining the task or recovery options.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Add persistent context outside the Loading State component describing the operation; use a more specific status pattern (modal, toast, or status page) for long waits that need explanation or cancellation options.";
    ds:guidelines "### Accessibility\n\n- Keep `role=\"status\"` and the off-screen `Loading...` label intact. The spinner is correctly `aria-hidden`, so state is not conveyed by animation alone.\n- `role=\"status\"` supplies polite live-region semantics. Do not wrap it in another competing status or alert that announces the same loading event.\n- The fixed message does not identify the affected region. Provide nearby context when multiple independent loading states can appear.\n- Do not move focus to the status; preserve focus on the initiating control or stable route destination.\n\n### Content\n\n- Use the separate Redirecting composition only when navigation, rather than data loading, is pending.\n- Pair long waits with useful visible context outside the spinner when users need to understand the operation or recovery path.\n- Do not add adjacent visible text that contradicts the fixed accessible `Loading...` status.\n\n### Responsive behavior\n\n- Use inline inside compact controls or copy and contained layout for a content region.\n- Reserve screen centering for a page-level wait state. Its source uses `height: 100vh` and `padding: 1rem`, with no small-viewport or dynamic-viewport override.\n- The default strip follows Vanilla layout. The component itself defines no width, breakpoint, or overflow rule.\n\n### Keyboard\n\n- Do not move focus to the spinner; preserve focus on the initiating control or next stable destination.\n- Loading State contains no interactive elements and must not be added to the tab order.\n- If pending work temporarily removes an interactive region, restore focus deliberately when stable content returns.\n\n### Internationalization\n\n- The accessible `Loading...` text is hardcoded English and cannot be customized through props. Localization requires a source API change.\n- The component has no visible copy, except when used by a separate composition such as Redirecting.\n- Ellipsis punctuation is part of the fixed source string; do not infer localization readiness from the icon-only visual presentation.\n\n";
    ds:tier ds:apps_landscape;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.specialadoption-docs;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`LoadingState.centerOnScreen`";
        ds:summary "Adds the full-viewport-height centering class to the outer non-inline wrapper. ";
        ds:propertyType "boolean";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "It does not add another element. Ignored when `inline` is truthy because the inline branch returns before wrapper rendering. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`LoadingState.inline`";
        ds:summary "Renders a bare status span instead of the contained strip structure. ";
        ds:propertyType "boolean";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Takes precedence over `centerOnScreen`; intended for compact placements. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ].
